# Public demo: stable Cloudflare named tunnel (preferred) or quick tunnel fallback.
#
# --- Named tunnel (stable hostname; set once in Vercel) ---
# 1. Run: ./scripts/setup_named_tunnel.sh
#    OR create a Zero Trust tunnel token and set CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN below.
# 2. Set PIXELFORGE_PUBLIC_API_URL to your fixed https hostname.
# 3. In Vercel production: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL = PIXELFORGE_PUBLIC_API_URL
#
# --- Quick tunnel (ephemeral; URL changes every restart) ---
#   cloudflared tunnel --url http://127.0.0.1:8000
#   Update Vercel NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL after each restart.

PIXELFORGE_CORS_ORIGINS=https://frontend-mu-two-wzuqjziue7.vercel.app,http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000

# Option A: Zero Trust install token (from Cloudflare dashboard → Tunnels)
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# Option B: Local cloudflared config from setup_named_tunnel.sh
# PIXELFORGE_CLOUDFLARED_CONFIG=/path/to/PixelForge/configs/cloudflared/config.yml

# Fixed public API URL (named tunnel only). Baked into Vercel at build time.
# PIXELFORGE_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
